---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '14 May 2026';
const effectiveDate = '14 May 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Tenderpreneurs"
  description="The terms that govern your use of the Tenderpreneurs service, including subscriptions, acceptable use, intellectual property, liability, and South African governing law."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <header class="mb-12 border-b border-slate-200 pb-8">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-slate-500">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">Terms of Service</h1>
      <dl class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-900">Effective:</dt> <dd class="inline">{effectiveDate}</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="inline font-medium text-slate-900">Last updated:</dt> <dd class="inline">{lastUpdated}</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-h2:mt-12 prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:font-semibold prose-a:text-slate-900 prose-a:underline prose-a:decoration-slate-400 prose-a:underline-offset-2">
      <p class="lead">
        These Terms of Service ("<strong>Terms</strong>") form a binding
        agreement between you and Tenderpreneurs (Pty) Ltd
        ("<strong>Tenderpreneurs</strong>", "we", "us") and govern your access
        to and use of the Tenderpreneurs website, mobile application, and
        related services (the "<strong>Service</strong>"). By creating an
        account or using the Service you agree to these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2 id="ect-notice">1. Information required by section 43 of the ECT Act</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Full name:</strong> Tenderpreneurs (Pty) Ltd</li>
        <li><strong>Place of registration:</strong> Republic of South Africa</li>
        <li><strong>Physical address:</strong> Western Cape, South Africa (available on written request)</li>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:hello@tenderpreneurs.co.za">hello@tenderpreneurs.co.za</a></li>
        <li><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://tenderpreneurs.co.za">https://tenderpreneurs.co.za</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="eligibility">2. Eligibility</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least 18 years old and able to enter into a binding
        contract. If you accept on behalf of a juristic person (company, close
        corporation, trust, NPC) you warrant that you are authorised to bind
        that entity.
      </p>

      <h2 id="account">3. Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for keeping your login credentials confidential and
        for all activity under your account. Notify us immediately at
        <a href="mailto:security@tenderpreneurs.co.za">security@tenderpreneurs.co.za</a>
        if you suspect unauthorised use.
      </p>

      <h2 id="subscription">4. Subscriptions, fees, and cancellation</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Subscription fees and billing cycles are shown on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>. Fees are inclusive of VAT where applicable.</li>
        <li>Subscriptions renew automatically until cancelled. You can cancel at any time from your account; cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing cycle.</li>
        <li>Except where required by the Consumer Protection Act, 2008 ("CPA") or the ECT Act, fees are non-refundable for partial periods.</li>
        <li>We may change pricing on 30 days' written notice. Continued use after the change takes effect constitutes acceptance of the new pricing.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="cooling-off">5. Cooling-off (where applicable)</h2>
      <p>
        If you are a natural person and you purchased a subscription as an
        electronic transaction within the meaning of the ECT Act, you may
        cancel within <strong>7 days</strong> after the date you first received
        access to the Service, in which case we will refund the fees paid
        within 30 days, less any direct costs of supplying the Service that you
        used during the cooling-off period.
      </p>

      <h2 id="acceptable-use">6. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Scrape, mirror, resell, or redistribute Service content except as permitted by your subscription tier;</li>
        <li>Reverse-engineer or attempt to derive source code from the Service;</li>
        <li>Use the Service to send unsolicited commercial communications in breach of POPIA or the CPA;</li>
        <li>Upload malicious code, attempt to gain unauthorised access, or interfere with the Service or its users;</li>
        <li>Use the Service for any unlawful purpose.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate accounts that breach this clause without
        refund.
      </p>

      <h2 id="ip">7. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Service, including all software, content, design, trade marks,
        and aggregated datasets, is owned by Tenderpreneurs or its licensors and
        is protected by South African and international intellectual property
        law. We grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable licence
        to use the Service for its intended purpose during your subscription.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tender notice text published by South African organs of state is
        government information and we do not claim ownership of it. Our
        aggregation, classification, summaries, and analyses are our own
        intellectual property.
      </p>

      <h2 id="disclaimer">8. No warranty of outcomes</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Important:</strong> Tenderpreneurs is an information and
        analytics service. We do not guarantee that you will be awarded any
        tender, that any tender we list will remain open or correctly
        described, or that any information sourced from third parties (such as
        the eTender Publication Portal or departmental websites) is complete or
        error-free. You must verify any tender directly with the issuing organ
        of state before bidding.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Service is provided "as is" and "as available". To the maximum
        extent permitted by law we exclude all implied warranties, save for the
        implied warranties of quality and fitness for purpose in section 55 of
        the CPA where the CPA applies.
      </p>

      <h2 id="liability">9. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability that cannot be
        excluded or limited by law (such as liability for fraud or for damage
        caused by gross negligence under section 51 of the CPA). Subject to
        that, our total aggregate liability arising out of or in connection
        with these Terms is limited to the fees you paid in the 12 months
        preceding the event giving rise to the claim. We are not liable for
        indirect, incidental, or consequential loss, including loss of profit,
        loss of business, or loss of data.
      </p>

      <h2 id="indemnity">10. Indemnity</h2>
      <p>
        You indemnify Tenderpreneurs against any third-party claim arising from
        your breach of these Terms or your use of the Service in violation of
        the law.
      </p>

      <h2 id="termination">11. Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate your access on reasonable notice for
        material breach, non-payment, or if required by law. On termination
        your right to use the Service ends; clauses that by their nature should
        survive (IP, liability, dispute resolution) survive termination.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to the Service or these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may change the Service or these Terms. Material changes will be
        communicated by email or an in-product notice at least 14 days before
        they take effect. Continued use after that date constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2 id="privacy">13. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our processing of your personal information is described in the
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which forms part of these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2 id="disputes">14. Disputes, governing law, and jurisdiction</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the law of the Republic of South Africa.
        Before formal proceedings, the parties will attempt to resolve any
        dispute by good-faith negotiation. Where the CPA applies and a dispute
        is not resolved, you may approach an accredited consumer ombud, the
        National Consumer Commission, or a consumer court. Otherwise, the
        parties consent to the non-exclusive jurisdiction of the Magistrates'
        Court having jurisdiction over Tenderpreneurs, even if the claim would
        ordinarily exceed that court's jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2 id="general">15. General</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Entire agreement:</strong> these Terms, the Privacy Policy, and the Cookies Policy form the entire agreement between us.</li>
        <li><strong>Severability:</strong> if any clause is found unenforceable, the rest remain in force.</li>
        <li><strong>Assignment:</strong> you may not assign these Terms without our written consent; we may assign on notice to you.</li>
        <li><strong>Notices:</strong> we may send notices to your account email; you may reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@tenderpreneurs.co.za">hello@tenderpreneurs.co.za</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
